The legal texts come from two sources:

  The Constitution and the Code of the Federated States of Micronesia, 2014 Edition (Annotated), as published by
  the FSM Legal Information System (https://www.fsmlaw.org), an Asian Development Bank project coordinated by the
  FSM Supreme Court, read from Internet Archive captures. This is an unofficial consolidation published by the FSM
  Legal Information System under the FSM Supreme Court; not an official publication. Its disclaimer says the copies
  "are not to be construed as an official publication".

  Public laws of the Federated States of Micronesia as published by the Congress of the Federated States of
  Micronesia (https://www.cfsm.gov.fm), retrieved 29 October 2026; the additional Congress 10–24 public-law documents were retrieved 3 November 2026.

Neither source states a licence. They are legal texts of the Federated States of Micronesia, reproduced with the
attribution above; their copyright status is not confirmed here.

Changes made by Lexifina: consolidated Code versions were converted to one Markdown file per provision, one paragraph
per line; spacing, quotes and dashes were normalised, and editorial annotations were left out. The additional enrolled
Congress laws each occupy a single file preserving the complete source word sequence, including printed line numbers
and administrative furniture, with whitespace normalised. Versions are arranged as git commits credited to their
sources. The wording of the law was not changed. Neither the FSM Legal Information System, the FSM Supreme Court nor
the Congress of the Federated States of Micronesia endorses this repository.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the tools) are
dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
